# Tests of the generic group that guest/xfstests.sh does not run, each with the
# reason. One "generic/NNN <reason>" per line. A test that cannot apply to a
# FUSE file system is not listed: xfstests' own _require_* checks make it "not
# run". These are tests that cannot be run in this guest at all (they fail or
# do not finish on the native file system too, or need something the busybox
# guest cannot carry) and tests that do not finish through dcfs in time, which
# is a finding about dcfs (the step 17.1 report), not a pass.
# The same list serves ext4, xfs and btrfs.
generic/001 takes 135 s through dcfs on ext4 (50 s natively), too close to the 200 s limit to be reliable
